Fixtures for tests/fit_test.py and tests/fit_test.sh.

models/<org>__<name>/
  config.json, tokenizer_config.json (and quantization_config.json where the repo has
  one) are the repo's own files at the revision in weights.json "source".
  weights.json is `console/fit.py fetch <repo> --revision <sha>` output, fetched
  2026-10-20: the tensor-class byte totals come from each weight file's header
  (safetensors data_offsets; GGUF tensor offsets), read with HTTP range requests.
  The pinned revisions are the ones the model-card digest of 2026-10-20 recorded
  (api.json "sha" of each repo). A GGUF repo has no config.json: its config.json and
  tokenizer_config.json come from the model card's base_model, recorded in
  weights.json "config_from".
  Re-fetch one: python3 console/fit.py fetch <repo> --revision <sha> --out <dir>

models/synthetic__huge-moe/
  Not a real model. Qwen3.8-Flash-Next's config.json with weights.json byte totals
  (1600 GiB of experts, 400 GiB n-gram table) that no fixture host can hold.

